'''''Survivor 51''''' is the upcoming fifty-first season of the American competitive reality television series [[Survivor (American TV series)|''Survivor'']]. It is scheduled to premiere in September 2026 on [[CBS]] in the [[United States]]. It was the nineteenth consecutive season to be filmed in the [[Mamanuca Islands]] in [[Fiji]].

==Production==
Ahead of the season 50 premiere, CBS renewed ''Survivor'' for its fifty-first season on January 22, 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |last=White |first=Peter |date=2026-01-22 |title='Survivor' & 'The Amazing Race' Renewed At CBS |url=https://deadline.com/2026/01/survivor-the-amazing-race-renewed-cbs-1236693430/ |access-date=2026-03-21 |website=Deadline |language=en-US}}</ref> A trailer was played at the ''[[Survivor 50: In the Hands of the Fans]]'' reunion, revealing that there will be 2 starting tribes, a first since ''[[Survivor: Winners at War|Winners at War]]''.<ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oSUzmg4zoLk |title=Survivor 51 {{!}} Sneak Peek |date=2026-05-20 |last=SurvivorOnCBS |access-date=2026-05-23 |via=YouTube}}</ref> This is the second season starting with an odd number of players, with 21, the first being ''[[Survivor: Fiji]]'' with 19 players.

==Contestants==
The 21 castaways were officially announced on August 25, 2026. Notable cast members include [[Devin Way]], a ''[[Grey's Anatomy]]'' and ''[[Queer as Folk (2022 TV series)|Queer as Folk]]'' actor and Brady Booker, a former [[WWE]] superstar.<ref name="parade">{{cite magazine|url=https://parade.com/tv/survivor-51-cast-2026 |title=''Survivor 51'' Cast Revealed: Meet the 21 New Contestants — Including a Former WWE Superstar and ''Grey’s Anatomy'' Star|magazine=Parade|last=Bloom|first=Mike|date=August 26, 2026|access-date=August 26, 2026}}</ref><ref name="EW">{{cite magazine|url=https://ew.com/survivor-51-cast-revealed-12068720 |title=Meet the cast of ''Survivor 51''|magazine=Entertaiment Weekly|last=Ross|first=Dalton|date=August 26, 2026|access-date=August 26, 2026}}</ref>

